Hi Folks,

The code:
> require(ggplot2)
> df = data.frame(x = c(1:360), y = sin(seq(0,2*pi*3,length.out = 360)))
> ggplot(df, aes(x=x, y=y)) + geom_line()
> ggsave("temp.wmf")
produces http://i.imgur.com/mjjSKih.png

temp.wmf file turns out to be bitmapped and not vectorized.  However, saving as .pdf produces vectors, not bitmaps.  Shouldn't .wmf files save as vectors also?

Thanks,
Allie

