Hi,

A tutorial mentioned the following to illustrate geom_bar:

qplot(clarity, data=diamonds, geom="bar", fill=cut, position="stack")
qplot(clarity, data=diamonds, geom="bar", fill=cut, position="dodge")
qplot(clarity, data=diamonds, geom="bar", fill=cut, position="fill")
qplot(clarity, data=diamonds, geom="bar", fill=cut, position="identity")

I was trying to reproduce the same using ggplot, and tried the following:
ggplot(diamonds) + geom_bar(aes(clarity,fill=cut,position="fill"))

However it does not produce the desired output. I then changed the above as follows, which works:
ggplot(diamonds, aes(clarity, fill=cut)) + geom_bar(position="fill")

What I do not understand is the difference between the two. I have searched old posts of the forum, but could not find anything that explains it.

Cheers !

